      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T06:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Questions about using real device assigning hypervisor (aosp/2854493):\n\n- Questions) Can we proceed booting when hypervisor is missing, if no device is assigned?\n  - If so, Should it be obtained in `entry.rs` and passed to `device_assignment.rs`? What about `device_assignment.rs` gets it by itself when necessary because hypervisor is singleton?",
      "revId": "65707aa24bc641d18b8c75fe11e309b810339430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23bd49d9_2febd8c1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-05T16:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, if `hyp::get_device_assigner().is_none()` and `vm_dtbo().is_some()`, we should log an error and skip the DA path but still boot (with all assigned devices stripped, naturally) as there\u0027s no reason to prevent non-DA VMs from booting; WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "bac8e132_aa508513",
      "revId": "65707aa24bc641d18b8c75fe11e309b810339430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a56b3c2_63de4da7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-06T17:02:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I asked the question because `hyp::get_device_assigner().is_none()` means no hypervisor. I thought that no hypervisor can be considered as \u0027strange enough to stop protected VM boot\u0027 even when `pvmfw` don\u0027t use hypervisor. Could you confirm if my understanding is correct from the security perspective?\n\nI just updated the code to obtain hypervisor in `device_assignment.rs`, assuming that no hypervisor is OK if unused in `pvmfw` (i.e. nothing is assigned). Tell me if my understanding is wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "23bd49d9_2febd8c1",
      "revId": "65707aa24bc641d18b8c75fe11e309b810339430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b49eec15_e83ce022",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-06T19:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `hyp::get_device_assigner().is_none()` means no hypervisor.\n\nNo, it means no `DeviceAssigningHypervisor` i.e. that the hypervisor doesn\u0027t support DA.\n\nFYI, at the point where pvmfw starts dealing with DA, it has already interacted with the hypervisor _a lot_ (for discovering which one it\u0027s running on (KVM/pKVM/Gunhya/GZ), sharing MMIO to access the virtual PCI bus, sharing memory for the VirtIO message passing) so all the code is written assuming that we have one. If pvmfw ([technically, vmbase](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/vmbase/src/entry.rs;l\u003d28;drc\u003d20daaefa0b70a5dd195540a5da8860b50c2e795b)) fails to detect a hypervisor it\u0027s familiar with, [it bails out](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/hyp/src/hypervisor.rs;l\u003d108;drc\u003dfb24bddbb17414f5ece58bd3560af57b87ee346d).\n\n\u003e assuming that no hypervisor is OK if unused in `pvmfw` (i.e. nothing is assigned)\n\nWe can\u0027t know that nothing has been assigned until the crosvm DT gets parsed by `DeviceAssignmentInfo::parse`, which should only be called if `get_device_assigner().is_some()` so my point was that if ABL passed us a VM DTBO (`vm_dtbo().is_some()`) but we detected that the hypervisor doesn\u0027t support DA (`get_device_assigner().is_none()`) then we shouldn\u0027t abort the boot as we might be booting a VM that doesn\u0027t have any assigned devices. So, instead, let\u0027s just log the inconsistency (for debug) and move on, skipping the rest of the DA code.\n\nBTW, note that aosp/2824757 makes `get_device_assigner()` **always** return `Some` because pKVM (unfortunately) doesn\u0027t provide a discovery mechanism for it. As a result, this code will always call `DeviceAssignmentInfo::parse` and pKVM/crosvm not supporting DA will only be detected at the point where the verification HVC is issued. This is why I was suggesting to temporarily ignore that function failing but, as you said in the other thread, that actually should never happen on ToT.\n\nSo, review comment: don\u0027t take the hypervisor by `Option` in `DeviceAssignmentInfo::parse`.",
      "parentUuid": "2a56b3c2_63de4da7",
      "revId": "65707aa24bc641d18b8c75fe11e309b810339430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
