      "writtenOn": "2023-12-07T10:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003e So, review comment: don\u0027t take the hypervisor by `Option` in `DeviceAssignmentInfo::parse`.\n\u003e\n\u003e Also, I need a way to inject `MockHypevisor` for testing -- that\u0027s why take hypervisor as platform\n\nSure, all I\u0027m saying is define\n```\npub fn parse(..., hypervisor: \u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor) -\u003e ...\n```\ninstead of\n```\npub fn parse(..., hypervisor: Option\u003c\u0026dyn DeviceAssigningHypervisor\u003e) -\u003e ...\n```\n\n\u003e What if a node in VM DTBO doesn\u0027t require physical `\u003creg\u003e` and `\u003ciommus\u003e` but assigned as if it\u0027s a device driver node?\n\nAssignment of platform devices basically boils down to donating MMIO memory from the host to the guest and mapping guest memory into device memory so if the DT node doesn\u0027t have either it 1. requires no MMIO donation and 2. is incapable of DMA so doesn\u0027t so isn\u0027t relevant for device assignment and shouldn\u0027t be in the VM DTBO? Do you have an example?\n\nSomething that could fit your description is a source of interrupts (but without MMIO, how do you program what triggers them?) handled through the vGIC but either the interrupts are generated by the host (the case today) and then should be considered virtual OR they\u0027re directly injected from the HV (not supported today) and would then also require validation.",
      "parentUuid": "ab60981c_9c21c0c0",
      "revId": "65707aa24bc641d18b8c75fe11e309b810339430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
